// Each guarantee names the other machine in a specification call. Neither
// proof cites the other guarantee: both bodies are the plain definition
// `value`, so the checked body summary of the callee proves each exit
// (state_contracts.md, local call summaries). No body is recursive, so no
// summary is assumed around a cycle. A false variant still rejects in
// fail/core/scoped_integer_call_guarantee_retains_actual.
machine first(value: i16) -> i16
ensures (second(value) as i16 in Saturating) == result { value }
machine second(value: i16) -> i16
ensures (first(value) as i16 in Wrapping) == result { value }
machine main() {}
